    },
    {
      "source": "L4",
      "pdfPage": 3,
      "anchor": "• A chemical bond is the force of attraction between two atoms;",
      "verification": "literal-text-match-in-authorised-local-PDF-extraction"
    },
    {
      "source": "L4",
      "pdfPage": 4,
      "anchor": "− Read: Born Haber Cycle and Hess Law of Constant Heat Summation",
      "verification": "literal-text-match-in-authorised-local-PDF-extraction"
    },
    {
      "source": "L4",
      "pdfPage": 5,
      "anchor": "− Electronegativity difference (high positive value)",
      "verification": "literal-text-match-in-authorised-local-PDF-extraction"
    },
    {
      "source": "L4",
      "pdfPage": 6,
      "anchor": "Na, O                      2.5                           Most ionic compound",
      "verification": "literal-text-match-in-authorised-local-PDF-extraction"
    },
    {
      "source": "L4",
      "pdfPage": 7,
      "anchor": "• The bond formation due to the sharing of electrons between",
      "verification": "literal-text-match-in-authorised-local-PDF-extraction"
    },
    {
      "source": "L4",
      "pdfPage": 8,
      "anchor": "orbitals along their internuclear lines. The internuclear line is the",
      "verification": "literal-text-match-in-authorised-local-PDF-extraction"
    },
    {
      "source": "L4",
      "pdfPage": 10,
      "anchor": "− This involves a side-to-side or lateral overlap of atomic orbitals",
      "verification": "literal-text-match-in-authorised-local-PDF-extraction"
    },
    {
      "source": "L4",
      "pdfPage": 11,
      "anchor": "− Note: π bonds are weaker and more reactive than σ bonds because π",
      "verification": "literal-text-match-in-authorised-local-PDF-extraction"
    },
    {
      "source": "L4",
      "pdfPage": 12,
      "anchor": "Has an impact on the shape of               Has no role in determining the",
      "verification": "literal-text-match-in-authorised-local-PDF-extraction"
    },
    {
      "source": "L4",
      "pdfPage": 13,
      "anchor": "be divalent because of 2 unpair electrons, but C is tetravalent because",
      "verification": "literal-text-match-in-authorised-local-PDF-extraction"
    },
    {
      "source": "L4",
      "pdfPage": 14,
      "anchor": "− sp hybridization: BeF2, BeH2, BeCl2, C2H2",
      "verification": "literal-text-match-in-authorised-local-PDF-extraction"
    },
    {
      "source": "L4",
      "pdfPage": 16,
      "anchor": "↑↓      ↑   ↑                              ↑             ↑   ↑     ↑",
      "verification": "literal-text-match-in-authorised-local-PDF-extraction"
    },
    {
      "source": "L4",
      "pdfPage": 18,
      "anchor": "− Note: there are 2 hybridized orbitals and 2 unhybridized orbitals;",
      "verification": "literal-text-match-in-authorised-local-PDF-extraction"
    },
    {
      "source": "L4",
      "pdfPage": 20,
      "anchor": "− Note: some essential body’s organic molecules contain coordinate",
      "verification": "literal-text-match-in-authorised-local-PDF-extraction"
    },
    {
      "source": "L4",
      "pdfPage": 23,
      "anchor": "− The donor atom, N, in NH3, can donate a lone pair of electrons and the",
      "verification": "literal-text-match-in-authorised-local-PDF-extraction"
    },
    {
      "source": "L4",
      "pdfPage": 24,
      "anchor": "− For a double bond, one is a sigma bond, and the other is a pi bond",
